> **The literal usernames/group names above are NOT predictable from this
> report.** BadBlood draws all of its randomness through PowerShell's
> `Get-Random`, seeded via `Get-Random -SetSeed` at deploy time on the
> Windows host itself — .NET's RNG algorithm differs from Python's, so the
> same integer seed does not reproduce the same name sequence here. Only the
> counts and the seed (for re-running BadBlood identically later) are known
> ahead of deployment. Query the live domain (`Get-ADUser -Filter *`) for the
> real names after `/deploy`.

