## Credentials

### Domain administrator

`Administrator` is the domain's real RID-500 account, not a fresh object —
promoting a domain's first DC seeds it from whatever local account did the
promotion (`local_admin_username` below, renamed to `Administrator` right
before promotion since Azure forbids that name as a VM's own admin_username).
Its password is therefore unchanged by promotion: the same password as
"Local VM administrator" below — which is also what this harness uses as
every host's DSRM/safe-mode password, so there is only the one password.
Verified against a real deploy that treating this as a distinct,
freshly-generated secret breaks both domain-join ("user name or password is
incorrect") and any later AD object management ("server has rejected the
client credentials").

